  "body": "### How to reproduce this bug?\n\nDuring the validation of this [change](https://github.com/weaviate/weaviate/pull/5516), it was found out that invoking `replace` for an object which is being deleted returns the following 500 error:\r\n```\r\nweaviate.exceptions.UnexpectedStatusCodeError: Object was not replaced.! Unexpected status code: 500, with response body: {'error': [{'message': \"no object with id '1f35fff0-4c66-48d5-9eed-b759fc3a48f6'\"}]}.\r\n```\r\nIn the PR linked at the beginning of this issue, the behavior was changed so that a 404 error would be returned in cases like this. To keep the APIs consistent, it would be good to modify this behavior, so that a 404 error would be returned, instead of a 500.\n\n### What is the expected behavior?\n\nReplacing (`collections.data.replace`) an object while it is being deleted should return a 404 error.\n\n### What is the actual behavior?\n\nReplacing (`collections.data.replace`) an object while it is being deleted returns a 500 error.\n\n### Supporting information\n\n_No response_\n\n### Server Version\n\n1.24.21\n\n### Code of Conduct\n\n- [X] I have read and agree to the Weaviate's [Contributor Guide](https://weaviate.io/developers/contributor-guide) and [Code of Conduct](https://weaviate.io/service/code-of-conduct)",
